{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1239393-2e-legacy-interpretation-tamers-of-the-cave","id":1239393,"title":"2E Legacy Interpretation: Tamers of the Cave","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-27T12:05:34-07:00","id":1239393,"title":"2E Legacy Interpretation: Tamers of the Cave","content":"So, a preface: this is going to break some Legacy Attainment assumptions.<br /> <br /> This is an update of the Tamers of the Cave from 1E. This strays heavily from conventional assumptions on the construction and power of attainments owing to the signature substance of the Legacy\u2014ether\u2014being limited and limiting, forcing attainments to work within its context. Given the role of the etheric mirror as a yantra even before they existed (in 1E it could function as another Dedicated Tool) and my own desire to give elemental meaning to it which was absent its description in 1E beyond that it was \u201cthe void,\u201d the Arcana involved have been altered slightly as well.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the attainments do not map neatly to other spells in their powers or effects. Breakdowns are provided after the Legacy. I will say I\u2019m not fond of how the basic attainments and optional powers are doing two different things, but the 1E Tamers of the Cave had that too and I was trying to reproduce their style. Might do another version where I rip out the wizard vomit and focus on their guidance and martyrdom concepts (probably Fate-primary).<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Tamers of the Cave</b></span><br /> <i>Background and further details can be found in </i>Legacies: the Ancient<br /> <br /> <i>Sobriquet:</i> Socratics<br /> <i>Parent Path and Order:</i> Mastigos, Elemental Tamers<br /> <i>Ruling Arcanum:</i> Death or Prime<br /> <br /> <i>Yantras: </i>Ether (+1), Socratic Debate (+2), Wound Penalties (+1-3, equal to penalty), Taking Risks for the Sake of Another (+1, +2 if a Sleeper), Facing Certain Death (+3)<br /> <i>Oblations:</i> Community service, fasting, meditation in a solitary place, mentoring<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b><br /> <i>Requirements:</i> Death 2, Prime 2, Mind 1, Occult 2, Empathy 1, Expression 1<br /> One must find or be noticed be a current Tamer of the Cave and show a sincere desire to follow the Legacy\u2019s desire for the improvement of the human condition through their own self-sacrificing martyrdom. A prospective Socratic meditates on paradoxical koans under the guidance of their mentor, fasts, and enters a state of near-death for three days. Upon coming out of the trance, they are now members of the Legacy, understanding and capable of calling on the element of the void. The Socratics, like with all the Tamers, view their role to help humanity, and their particular brand of it calls for an ability to understand and be understood by others. A philosophical understanding of Socrates is valued, but not necessary.<br /> <br /> Both Death and Prime are required for the Legacy\u2019s attainments. Moros may choose Prime as a Path Arcanum, while all other Paths learn Death.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attainments</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><u>Conversation</u></i><br /> Some of the Optional abilities of the Attainments require the Socratic to engage and remain in conversation. This is defined as in a state of engagement in which no non-reflexive actions may be taken except for those associated with Social Maneuvering, such as the Legacy\u2019s attainments or certain spells cast with conversational yantras and Imagoes (pointed looks, insightful phrases, etc). Given the potentially-long, potentially-time-compressing nature of Social Maneuvering, basic necessities such as sleeping, eating, or bathroom breaks do not break conversation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u><i>Initiation: Etheric Communion</i></u></b><br /> A Socratic emerges from their death-trance transformed, linked with and understanding the power and value of nothingness; all springs of it, all returns to it. It is meaning. They are capable of secreting starry ether from their orifices as an instant action, similar to the Death spell \u201cEctoplasm,\u201d though it is incapable of being used for Manifestations. At this stage the viscous substance cannot be shaped, only smeared (such as on the surface of a mirror). If used in spellcasting, it can function as a Dedicated Tool. The ether vanishes after a scene, or once it has been used in a spell as a yantra.<br /> <br /> <i>Optional: </i>Mind 1, Empathy 1<br /> The Socratic must understand others to guide and inspire them. This duplicates the Mind spell \u201cMental Scan\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u><i>Second: From Nothing, Something</i></u></b><br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> Gnosis 2, Death 2, Prime 2, Expression 2<br /> With an instant action, the Socratic may shape their conjured ether into solid forms, similar to the Death spell \u201cShape Ephemera.\u201d This lasts until the ether vanishes, either at the end of the scene or when it is used as a yantra. When ether is now used as a yantra in spellcasting, the spellcasting roll gains the benefit of 9-Again.<br /> <br /> <i>Optional:</i> Mind 2, Empathy 2<br /> Through a disarming smile, an intimidating glare, or a placid look suggesting utmost empathy, the Socratic understands enough of others to put them at-ease with them even during the direst of circumstances. As an instant action, the Socratic can improve their first impression by the subject by levels equal to its primary factor of Potency. This is Withstood by Composure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u><i>Third: Etheric Doorway</i></u></b><br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> Gnosis 4,Death 3, Prime 3, Occult 3<br /> The Socratic smears ether across a portal\u2014such as a sizable mirror or door\u2014or on a surface into the shape of a doorframe. As an instant action, the Socratic turns this into an Etheric Doorway, lasting several turns. Anyone or anything passing through the gateway enters Twilight as a faded, faintly-starry version of itself. This state is capable of perceiving and physically interacting with all forms of Twilight, and vice-versa. Disembodied souls are visible but remain insubstantial without the use of further magic.<br /> <br /> <i>Optional:</i> Mind 3, Empathy 3<br /> Sometimes called \u201cthe Inescapable Question,\u201d with one sentence and 1 point of Mana the Socratic can begin the process of turning enemies into friends, allies into betrayers, and doubters into acolytes. The Socratic asks the subject of this Attainment a question, forcing them into a moment of evaluation. For as long as the Socratic maintains conversation with the subject\u2014typically in the form of Socratic debate\u2014the subject endures the Beaten Down Tilt. This can go on for days or weeks, the participants pausing only to tend to their needs, and is used as much to prevent fights from happening as it is to stop them. This Attainment is Withstood by Wits, its Primary Factor is Potency, and benefits from Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u><i>Fourth: Etheric Transfiguration</i></u></b><br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> Gnosis 6, Death 4, Prime 4<br /> Sometimes mistaken as the final Attainment of the Tamers of the Cave, they become the ether. The Socratic meditates for a scene, reentering the death trance from their initiation. At the end, ether issues from their orifices, covering them and transfiguring them into a being of pure ether. In this state they may use the Legacy\u2019s previous attainments on themselves, taking an instant action to function as an Etheric Doorway for others, to shift into Twilight themselves, or to alter their forms with \u201cFrom Something, Nothing.\u201d They might flatten their forms to fit beneath doors, shape their limbs into tools or weapons, or change their shape to appear less human.<br /> <br /> The Socratic may remain in this state for up to three days, requiring no food, drink, or sleep. Those willing to explore deeper mysteries of the void, or commit themselves wholly to a cause or action, may shed their mortal coil and persist as etheric shades for a month, disappearing completely once the attainment ends. This extends to a year at Death/Prime 5.<br /> <br /> <i>Optional: </i>Mind 4, Empathy 4<br /> The Socratic can force others to revisit and reflect on their actions or share their own for the sake of teaching. With a few words or a gesture, the Socratic and the subject are transported into a moment from either\u2019s memories, one intended to evoke a specific emotion. They can wander about this illusion, remembering the smell of flowers or feeling the coldness of snow, but to observers both subjects remain where they were, still conversing. In the event of physical confrontation, calculate traits and consequences as dream forms. This opens or closes one Door for the Duration, which can end abruptly should the Socratic cease conversation or they are \u201ckilled.\u201d This Attainment is Withstood by Composure, its primary factor is Potency, and benefits from Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u><i>Fifth: Apostle and Tomb</i></u></b><br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> Gnosis 8, Death 5, Prime 5<br /> The Socratic meditates for a scene, reconnecting with the death trance of his initiation like in <i>Etheric Transfiguration.</i> Unlike the previous attainment, at the climax the Socratic spend 1 Mana and suffers 1 Resistant Aggravated level of damage as they rip their etheric form away from themselves, creating a mindless apostle similar to the Prime spell \u201cEidolon.\u201d The Apostle possesses a Structure equal to the Socratic\u2019s Gnosis, the ability to be the subject of the Legacy\u2019s previous attainments (as <i>Etheric Transfiguration</i>), a Connected sympathetic link, and functions as a 5-dot Retainer for a week after which it fades back into nothing.<br /> <br /> What isn\u2019t widely known is that, should the Socratic die during this time, the Apostle immediately becomes an Anchor for their ghost and is considered Open by the Socratic. This may be the source of some of the strangest rumors of the Legacy, that they sometimes rise from the dead and leave no ghost.<br /> <br /> <i>Optional: </i>Mind 5<br /> The Apostle, in its base state, may be endowed with intelligence and self-awareness, allowing it to more faithfully serve its creator in its role as retainer or participant in their passion play. The Apostle gains traits and essence as a Rank 1 goetia, the Mortal Mask numina, and can now choose to take advantage of the Legacy\u2019s Attainments on its own, shaping itself, shifting itself and others into Twilight as needed, and engaging in debate. It cannot duplicate <i>Apostle and Tomb</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b><u>Design Breakdown</u></b></i><br /> I wanted to try my hand at some of those attainments mentioned in the core that are mentioned as impossible to develop praxes for. Them not mapping to arcana is part of the point.<br /> The first attainment somewhat mimics a Death 2 spell, but the inability to shape it or use it for ghostly manifestations I think puts it in the first attainment category. It functioning as a dedicated tool was in 1E, and I think Prime suits that well enough. The secondary power is just a basic, instant Mind spell.<br /> <br /> The second attainment mimics the Death 2 spell Shape Ephemera with more Reach than would otherwise be possible; I feel its effects are justified given it is limited to ether, and its tendency to vanish during spellcasting. The 9-again mimics As Above, So Below, but persistent specifically to ether; again, I feel this limitation justifies it, and the Socratic needs to barf up some more as an instant action each time he wants to cast with it anyway. The secondary power is Mind 2\u2019s First Impressions with the primary factor changed; this is a personal choice, since I feel any spell with a Withstand not having Potency as its primary is ridiculous. If you'd rather run it more orthodox, just assign the Reach to swapping factors and give it an activation set-up of a scene since it's already meant to be used as part of lengthy debates.<br /> <br /> The third attainment is modeled off of Ghost Gate but utilizes conjunctional Prime to attune users to a universal Twilight. I don\u2019t feel it\u2019s a stretch, given Prime already possessed the ability to make something capable of interacting with all layers of Twilight. The secondary power is a custom Ruling spell. Ruling is capable of inflicting Conditions and Tilts, and Mind Armor can already inflict Beaten Down. The mana cost and requirement to remain in conversation are there to keep it from just being a tool to whittle down an opponent\u2019s WP. The conversational element is more restrictive than what is \u201cneeded\u201d to balance it, but it matches the Legacy\u2019s aesthetics and synergizes with the third and fourth secondaries.<br /> <br /> The fourth attainment superficially resembles Death 4\u2019s Shadow Flesh. Prime element is just that you\u2019re a mutable ether person who benefits from all his attainments. Secondary power is a bit hard to pin down: it resembles some combination of Mind\u2019s Emotional Urging, Dream Reaching, and Hallucination. The mechanical effect is from Emotional Urging, the aesthetics are more the other two. Unlike Hallucination, the Mage is part of the experience too. Unlike Dream Reaching, the conversational element makes it easy for the subject to end the effect. I believe these mitigating factors, along with the mechanical effect being from a Mind 2 spell, justifies dressing things up for drama since the only extra advantage this might confer comes from the narrative.<br /> <br /> Fifth attainment is just Prime 5\u2019s Eidolon, slightly different and costlier\u20141 resistant aggravated isn\u2019t anything to sneer at. The Death effect doesn\u2019t really have a precedented spell, but cut the guy some slack, they\u2019re a second-degree Master and they\u2019re dead. They\u2019ve only got a week left at most. The secondary power is just adding Mind 5\u2019s Psychic Genesis to it, something Eidolon already had available as a conjunctional effect. Numina are Mortal Mask and their Attainments. An argument could be made that this might be a bridge too far, but the character is a third-degree Master with Gnosis 8 and by that point their servant having the arguable equivalent of 1 extra numina is the power equivalent of complaining about acne on a leper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T16:26:10-07:00","id":1239471,"title":"","content":"Ooh, looks nice. Although one worry is that requiring two (three for Optionals) Arcana to advance might be a little heavy. Which reminds me, I need to revisit my own homebrew take on the Elemental Masteries...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T17:23:44-07:00","id":1239485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1239393-2e-legacy-interpretation-tamers-of-the-cave?p=1239471#post1239471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, looks nice. Although one worry is that requiring two (three for Optionals) Arcana to advance might be a little heavy. Which reminds me, I need to revisit my own homebrew take on the Elemental Masteries...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fond of multiple-primary Legacies, like the Celestial Masters and Uncrowned Kings.In this case, though, it really was just because it was the only way I could think to make sense of their ether goop and stretch it out for five entire attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T18:40:13-07:00","id":1239514,"title":"","content":"Oh, I meant more in terms of Exp needed, rather than the Ruling Arcana setup. But yeah, 1E Attainments are often tricky to convert to the 2E frame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T20:35:28-07:00","id":1239541,"title":"","content":"Read it over, and I don't think there's anything missing here. I have a kneejerk reaction that says there should be Reached assigned to Sensory for the Mind attainments, but you have to be engaged in &quot;conversation,&quot; and it only appears to work on one person at a time so I think it balances out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T21:57:11-07:00","id":1239562,"title":"","content":"Yeah, first pass had me trying to fit sensory in, leaning more into the idea of this being something intended for scenes of subjective time. It broke down a bit because it made it possible to use most of them not as social aids, but ways to troll people in combat (constantly inflicting Beaten Down at no risk to whittle opponents' Willpower to nothing, trapping them in illusion realms) rather than be aids in the entire idea of guiding pupils and debating enemies.<br /> <br /> Conversation fixed (in my mind, anyway) those exploitative elements and funneled their use into the desired implementation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T16:16:28-07:00","id":1239822,"title":"","content":"A bit late, but if anyone wants a good idea of a source of inspiration I was partially pulling from, go check out the <i>Karnak</i> miniseries by Warren Ellis. Specifically, issue 5 and the character of Russoff the Painter. As well as the fate he meets.<br /> <br /> Edit: The <i>Karnak</i> miniseries is itself probably a pretty good source of inspiration for Mage on its own merits, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 07-28-2018, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}